  "term": "coercive behavior",
  "definition": "Coercive behavior is a repeated pattern in a close relationship in which one person uses pressure, intimidation, control, or force against a partner or spouse. It can occur along with physical, psychological, or sexual abuse, as well as isolation, stalking, deprivation, or reproductive control.",
